  "body": "## Change and mathematical scope\n\n**Independent verification / scoped negative result; no new kappa.** This package independently corroborates the cost-64 floor for P112 masked root-star decoders with exact `C(alpha)` / self-trimmed `N(alpha)` supports, arbitrary complex coefficients, any finite term count and free rank-zero corrections.\n\nThe final overlap refresh found David Arias's #1236, which had already submitted the same theorem while this work was underway. Credit belongs to that concurrent submission; this PR adds independent evidence, not a stronger theorem or priority claim. Navinor's #1226 supplies the preceding support-family census and assembly question.\n\nThe distinct implementation generates E8 roots by Weyl reflections, checks pairing ranks by column elimination and exhausts maximal cliques with pivoted Bron-Kerbosch. It imports neither predecessor code nor the new primary checker. The primary checker separately reconstructs roots, uses row elimination and enumerates every clique. Both reconstruct all 57,600 ordered support-pair costs and 1,260 frames, verify frame annihilation and extension, exclude nine compatible live normals, and check the cost-64 coordinate decoder on all 12,544 entries. The independent maximal-clique census is `{3: 896, 7: 23040, 8: 4032}`.\n\nThis also supplies a successful **Python 3.12.13 registered-package replay of #1236 at `ee8437bd9879272094e20c024cd34a53c4e84cd8`**, including all seven package tests. Its initial validation note recorded that environment as untested. Eight shared mathematical certificate fields agree exactly.\n\n## Task and overlap\n\nSeed **36**, complex-supplier track; base **`49b3157d1d89adcef16df8be98445451672be5ba`**. Card `complex-masked-decoder`, refined to #1226's assembly gap and finally labeled independent corroboration after finding #1236. The initial local claim records three candidate tasks. No pinned sprint issue existed.\n\nThe refreshed overlap search covered 843 open PRs and 14 indexed discussion records with complete pagination, followed by a latest-PR check through #1240. Exact heads and source hashes are in `SOURCES.json`; the local claim was updated with the result and artifact link. #1212/#1213/#1191 and #1224 are credited as adjacent work and are not proof dependencies.\n\n## Validation\n\nOne offline replay command, Python 3.10+ with the standard library:\n\n```sh\npython3 -I -B research/masked-star-frame-compatibility/test_package.py\n```\n\nExpected final marker: `PASS_MASKED_STAR_PACKAGE`. The package passes on CPython 3.14.6 and through the repository's registered Python 3.12.13 runner. Seven semantic controls pass; both checkers reject three corrupted certificates. Optimized isolated relocation to a path containing spaces passes and preserves the certificate. The pinned #1226 census, package metadata/source pins, selected-record integrity and staged whitespace checks also pass. Exact commands, outputs and source hashes are in `VALIDATION.json`.\n\nOnly `research/masked-star-frame-compatibility/` is added. The selected frontier, upstream and frozen predecessors are unchanged. No native supplier/cold replay, repository-wide historical suite, Lean proof or hosted CI success is claimed by the local receipt. All inherited physical/compiler, hosting, precision/tape and analytic obligations remain. Further trims, arbitrary subsets, other punctures and shared-copy pricing are outside this floor.\n\n## Credit and next questions\n\nPrepared by Hanson Sun (@bbMisk), with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance in proof development, both implementations, experiments and writing. Independent implementations within an AI-assisted contribution are not independent human review. Apache-2.0. README credits David Arias / #1236, Navinor / #1226, DreamingOfClouds, themilkman216, woklerx, GamingPuzzled and adjacent contributions individually.\n\nREADME and TASK.json record the remaining question: whether an additional live-line trim changes the atom-rank and missed-frame constraints. That enlarged family has no favorable complete supplier budget or legal realization established here.\n",
